# STAGE-4 NEW (critique items #11, #12): inlined from calibration_and_significance.py.
# A full search of the previous pipeline found NO implementation of Brier
# score, ECE, McNemar's test, or a real (resampling) bootstrap CI, even
# though the paper describes all four. What WAS implemented is a 1.96*SEM
# normal-approximation "95% CI" across repeated-CV repeats, and a paired
# t-test (not Wilcoxon) of each ablation view vs the Full view - legitimate,
# but a different question than calibration or pairwise McNemar comparison
# on one shared test set. These functions are called once per project from
# run_pipeline, right after the feature-importance block.
